          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Quantum hadrodynamics is (or should be) an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            that describes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron"} hadron
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states"} bound states
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+physics"} nuclear physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and specifically with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleons"} nucleons
          %p
            In this sense
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
            is the archetype of quantum hadrodynamics, but the latter term is commonly used more specifically for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walecka+model"} Walecka model
            and its generalizations (QHD-I
            %a{:href => "#Walecka74"} Walecka 74
            and QHD-II
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Serot79"} Serot 79
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#SerotWalecka92"} Serot-Walecka 92
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SerotWalecka97"} Serot-Walecka 97
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon+chiral+perturbation+theory"} baryon chiral perturbation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            and specifically the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleons"} nucleons
            appear as explicit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            (as opposed to as emergent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
            fields).
